==Description==

The [[Image:Part_LinkArrayPoint.svg|24px]] '''Part LinkArrayPoint''' command creates a [[App_Link|Link]] array from a selected object by placing copies at the points of a selected shape.

The command can be used on many 3D objects such as those created with the [[Part_Workbench|Part Workbench]], but also on assembly instances created with the [[Assembly_Workbench|Assembly Workbench]].

== Usage ==

# Optionally select one object.
# There are several ways to invoke the command:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Part_LinkArrayPoint.svg|16px]] [[Part_LinkArrayPoint|Point Link Array]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Part/Assembly → Link Arrays → [[Image:Part_LinkArrayPoint.svg|16px]] Point Link Array}} option from the menu.
# The {{MenuCommand|Point Link Array}} task panel opens. See [[#Options|Options]] for more information.
# If you have not yet selected an object, press the {{Button|Select Object}} button and select one object.
# Enter the required parameters in the task panel.
# Press the {{Button|OK}} button to finish the command.

== Options ==

* Press the {{Button|Select Point Object}} button to select the shape with the points used for the array.
* Press the {{Button|Cancel}} button to abort the command.


